# Build output
/target
/target-docker
/target-amd64

# Local runtime: config, logs, the daemon keypair, downloaded torrents
/data/
*.log

# Docker environment, holds the Web UI password
.env

# Tooling caches
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editor leftovers
*~
.DS_Store

# The Web UI's icons, which are not optional.
#
# Many macOS global ignore files carry `Icon?`, meant for the `Icon\r` resource
# file the Finder writes. That pattern has no slash, so git applies it at every
# level, and on a case-insensitive filesystem git matches ignore patterns
# case-insensitively too: it matches the directory `icons`. All fifty-six icons
# were silently absent from the repository because of it, so a clone had an
# interface with no icons at all and only a fresh checkout could show it.
#
# The directory has to be re-included before its contents: git will not look
# inside an excluded directory.
!crates/redeluge-web/assets/icons/
!crates/redeluge-web/assets/icons/**
